{"raw": {"https://www.sf.edu/job/student-success-coordinator/": {"title": "Student Success Coordinator", "description": "Student Success Coordinator - University of Saint Francis, Fort Wayne Discover a path that's right for you. Find a Program Close 1. Location Fort Wayne Crown Point Indianapolis Lafayette Gas City Online Hybrid 2. Degree Level Bachelors Masters Associate Doctorate Licensure Certificate 3. Area(s) of interest/Pathways Allied Health Pathway Business and Leadership Pathway Creative Arts and Digital Media Pathway Education, Human Services and Community Care Pathway Humanities, Faith and Liberal Arts Pathway Nursing Pathway Sciences and Medical Studies Pathway Clear filters See programs 73 Programs Locations Cost & Aid Admissions Faith Campus Life About Visit Apply Give Search Faculty Directory Offices and Departments Search When autocomplete results are available use up and down arrows to review and enter to go to the desired page. Touch device users, explore by touch or with swipe gestures. Open Menu Close Menu Programs Locations Cost & Aid Admissions Faith Campus Life About Visit Apply Give Request Information LOCATION: Fort Wayne The University of Saint Francis is excited to announce the search for our next Student Success Coordinator. The University of Saint Francis in Fort Wayne, Indiana invites inquiries, nominations, and applications for the position of a Student Success Coordinator. Saint Francis is a Catholic, Franciscan university in the liberal arts tradition. The Student Success Coordinator will report to the Vice President for Student Life and Athletics and will have responsibility in student success, ensuring the university\u2019s Catholic identity, Franciscan charism, and commitment to the liberal arts remain at the center of our educational mission and public identity. The Student Success Coordinator is responsible for assisting the Vice President for Student Life and Athletics in advancing the university\u2019s efforts in implementing the new mission statement and strategic plan. The successful candidate should have experience in handling disability/accommodation requests as directed by the ADA/504 section of the of the Rehabilitation Act. The new Student Success Coach is expected to begin serving no later than December 1 st , 2026. Interested applicants should complete the online application, and include a cover letter, a resume, and the contact information for three references. The cover letter should directly address the responsibilities of the position with special emphasis placed upon the candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience as well as how the applicant will seek to advance the Catholic, Franciscan Mission of the University. Finalists may be required to provide official transcripts. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled; applications received before October 19 th , 2026 will be given full consideration. The University of Saint Francis offers formation of the whole person by providing an encounter with the heart and mind of Jesus Christ so that God, who is Love, may be loved. Through our Catholic identity, Franciscan charism, and liberal arts tradition, we prepare students for personal and professional lives of virtue, service, and joy. USF core values are the standards of behavior for every member of the university. They reflect those of the Sisters of Saint Francis of Perpetual Adoration and bring their charism to the university. Ceaseless Adoration \u2013 We adore God and interact with others in a way that honors His Presence. Generous Love \u2013 we spend time in community, give of ourselves, and accept help from others. Franciscan Joy \u2013 we delight in the simple things and give thanks in all circumstances. The University of Saint Francis promotes and celebrates the Catholic identity and Franciscan charism of the institution with an invitation to students, faculty and staff of all faiths. This God-centered and student-focused approach invites all employees to be a part of the formation of the whole person (students and colleagues) in a learning and working environment where character development and faith formation are as essential as academic achievement. Molding well-rounded, faith-filled, ethical leaders is the essence of the university\u2019s approach and all employees are expected to engage in a way that fulfills and furthers the mission. The university\u2019s strategic plan can be found at: https://be.sf.edu/renew-2028/ Job Description To apply for this job please visit app.frevvo.com . Academic Catalog Academic Calendar Alumni Athletics Camps Campus Store Campus Map Employment Events Event Services Library News \u00a9 2026 University of Saint Francis. All rights reserved. 2701 Spring Street | Fort Wayne, IN 46808 260-399-7700 | sf.edu Privacy Policy Title IX Student Consumer Disclosure CARES Act Funding"}, "https://www.sf.edu/job/payroll-and-benefits-administrator/": {"title": "Payroll and Benefits Administrator", "description": "Payroll and Benefits Administrator - University of Saint Francis, Fort Wayne Discover a path that's right for you. Find a Program Close 1. Location Fort Wayne Crown Point Indianapolis Lafayette Gas City Online Hybrid 2. Degree Level Bachelors Masters Associate Doctorate Licensure Certificate 3. Area(s) of interest/Pathways Allied Health Pathway Business and Leadership Pathway Creative Arts and Digital Media Pathway Education, Human Services and Community Care Pathway Humanities, Faith and Liberal Arts Pathway Nursing Pathway Sciences and Medical Studies Pathway Clear filters See programs 73 Programs Locations Cost & Aid Admissions Faith Campus Life About Visit Apply Give Search Faculty Directory Offices and Departments Search When autocomplete results are available use up and down arrows to review and enter to go to the desired page. Touch device users, explore by touch or with swipe gestures. Open Menu Close Menu Programs Locations Cost & Aid Admissions Faith Campus Life About Visit Apply Give Request Information Payroll and Benefits Administrator LOCATION: Fort Wayne The University of Saint Francis is excited to announce the search for our next Payroll and Benefits Administrator. The University of Saint Francis in Fort Wayne Indiana invites inquiries, nominations, and applications for the position of Payroll and Benefits Administrator Saint Francis is a Catholic, Franciscan university in the liberal arts tradition. The Payroll and Benefits Administrator will report to Director of Human Resources and will have responsibility over the area(s) of Payroll and Benefits ensuring the university\u2019s Catholic identity, Franciscan charism, and commitment to the liberal arts remain at the center of our educational mission and public identity. The Payroll and Benefits Administrator is responsible for assisting the Human Resources department in advancing the university\u2019s efforts in implementing the new mission statement and strategic plan. The successful candidate will demonstrate ownership and accountability, proactively identify and resolve discrepancies, approach employees with patience and service-mindedness, maintain accuracy under tight payroll deadlines, continuously seek process improvements and efficiencies, and stays current on employment law and compliance requirements. Interested applicants should complete the online application, and include a cover letter, a resume, and the contact information for three references. The cover letter should directly address the responsibilities of the position with special emphasis placed upon the candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience as well as how the applicant will seek to advance the Catholic, Franciscan Mission of the University. Finalists may be required to provide official transcripts. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled; applications received before October 9 th , 2026, will be given full consideration. The University of Saint Francis offers formation of the whole person by providing an encounter with the heart and mind of Jesus Christ so that God, who is Love, may be loved. Through our Catholic identity, Franciscan charism, and liberal arts tradition, we prepare students for personal and professional lives of virtue, service, and joy. USF core values are the standards of behavior for every member of the university. They reflect those of the Sisters of Saint Francis of Perpetual Adoration and bring their charism to the university. Ceaseless Adoration \u2013 We adore God and interact with others in a way that honors His Presence. Generous Love \u2013 we spend time in community, give of ourselves, and accept help from others. Franciscan Joy \u2013 we delight in the simple things and give thanks in all circumstances. The University of Saint Francis promotes and celebrates the Catholic identity and Franciscan charism of the institution with an invitation to students, faculty and staff of all faiths. This God-centered and student-focused approach invites all employees to be a part of the formation of the whole person (students and colleagues) in a learning and working environment where character development and faith formation are as essential as academic achievement. Molding well-rounded, faith-filled, ethical leaders is the essence of the university\u2019s approach and all employees are expected to engage in a way that fulfills and furthers the mission. The university\u2019s strategic plan can be found at: https://be.sf.edu/renew-2028/ Job Description To apply for this job please visit app.frevvo.com . ^ Academic Catalog Academic Calendar Alumni Athletics Camps Campus Store Campus Map Employment Events Event Services Library News \u00a9 2026 University of Saint Francis. All rights reserved. 2701 Spring Street | Fort Wayne, IN 46808 260-399-7700 | sf.edu Privacy Policy Title IX Student Consumer Disclosure CARES Act Funding Notifications <img height=\"1\" width=