oad is 12 credit hours per semester (fall and spring). Other responsibilities include providing effective leadership in curriculum development, implementation, evaluation, and staffing of the graduate programs, and coordinating with related programs, as well as continuing professional development and a commitment to collaboration and service within the Pathway, across the University and in the community.\u00a0 The successful candidate must be able to advance the Catholic and Franciscan Mission of the University. Rank and salary are dependent upon the appointee\u2019s qualifications and experience. A master\u2019s degree in an area of business is required; terminal degree is preferred for this position. Interested applicants should complete the online application, and include a letter of application, a CV, and the contact information for three references. The letter of application should directly address the responsibilities of the position with special emphasis placed upon the candidate\u2019s teaching experience and ability as well as how the applicant will seek to advance the Catholic, Franciscan Mission of the University. Finalists will be required to provide official transcripts. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled; applications received before June 5 th , 2026 will be given full consideration. The University of Saint Francis offers formation of the whole person by providing an encounter with the heart and mind of Jesus Christ so that God, who is Love, may be loved. Through our Catholic identity, Franciscan charism, and liberal arts tradition, we prepare students for personal and professional lives of virtue, service, and joy. USF core values are the standards of behavior for every member of the university. They reflect those of the Sisters of Saint Francis of Perpetual Adoration and bring their charism to the university. Ceaseless Adoration \u2013 We adore God and interact with others in a way that honors